ratory  about the viruses they do have  and what work they've been doing with  them  then there was another allegation about  the institute that surfaced more than a  year later  what u.s intelligence officials  learned is that there were three  researchers  who became ill enough to seek hospital  care they had symptoms that were like  coveted but the symptoms  like covet are also like flu symptoms  and flu was definitely circulating in  wuhan at that time  four days after the intelligence report  about the sick lab workers  the biden administration ordered a u.s  intelligence inquiry into the two  scenarios  china said the report was untrue  some people don't believe china and say  this has to be a cover-up  others say we just need to verify  that's what we do in science we verify  we look at the data  and reach our own conclusion it really  does boil down to  a question of transparency so for any  progress to be made in the origins of  the virus  it'll ultimately require more data and  fuller access to where it was first  detected  in china
 

